Use `ConfigureLifecycleEvents` in `MauiProgram.cs`:

```csharp
builder.ConfigureLifecycleEvents(events =>
{
#if ANDROID
    events.AddAndroid(android => android
        .OnPause(activity =>
        {
            // App lost focus (e.g., notification shade pulled down)
        })
        .OnStop(activity =>
        {
            // App fully backgrounded
        }));
#elif IOS || MACCATALYST
    events.AddiOS(ios => ios
        .DidEnterBackground(app =>
        {
            // App entered background
        }));
#endif
});
```

**Key points:**

- `OnPause` maps to MAUI's `Deactivated` (lost focus, may still be visible)
- `OnStop` and `DidEnterBackground` both map to MAUI's `Stopped` (fully backgrounded)
- Keep handlers fast (<5s on Android, limited time on iOS) to avoid ANR/watchdog kills

**Cross-platform alternative:** If you don't need platform-specific APIs, override `OnStopped()` on a `Window` subclass — it fires on all platforms when the app backgrounds:

```csharp
protected override void OnStopped()
{
    base.OnStopped();
    Preferences.Set("draft", _vm.Draft);
}
```
